      "value": "Ron, you say \"because new users\"\n\nIsn't this sort of why the hub existed in the first place?\nIsn't this why there was a tutorial?\n\nIf a new user ignores those, then don't coddle them, that's their own fault, this is a SOCIAL game, they can more than ask the nearest hub user. (or look at those helpful tips that used to be there. despite it's issues, I think the old new hub was fairly helpful in the \"helpful advice\" matter)\n\nBarring that, considering you added the VRchat home, shouldnt that be a tutorial there? Or  a tip added there? Perhaps near that little avatar selection and that mirror you can't turn off?\n\nIf the new user is going to by default load into the vrchat home, stick all the relevant \"new user\" handholdy stuff there for the easily lost.\n\nIt just makes no sense to add such redundancy to the menus, much less make it expanded by default.\n\nWhat was the point of adding the \"avatar worlds\" tab to the world list?\n\nWhere'd you find these focus testers? Reminds me of \"square peg in round hole\" valve playtesters",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
