      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "5ced99e664a53e191fbaae5e",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I don't see any positive impact for having worlds being listed in the social and avatar tab. A lot of people like myself and many of my friends have complained about the amount of lag that occurs when caching the thumbnails for said aforementioned worlds. This is also a bit redundant because we also have the Worlds Tab where all of the avatar worlds are listed regardless and it just muddies up the experience and makes the game feel clunky. If VRChat wants to keep with the avatar worlds being in the avatar menu i feel like that is okay, but it should at least be restricted to 5 worlds instead of the already expanded tab of over 10+. The menu is enough to crash my game when in an overpopulated world, and the lag it causes makes video players stutter audio sources and its just a mess.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Worlds in social and avatar menu lags more and seems redundant.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b8f1c2310e2de74d651b3c8",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've always had issues previously with the already existing In Room, Friend Requests, Online, Offline and the three new Group tabs which load everyone whether they're online or offline. \n\nJust as Jason mentioned above, my game also almost crashes as it buffers consistently for about a minute or two whenever I open my Social menu up, and that's an issue in just any world for me, but becomes a lot worse in overpopulated worlds. \n\nI really think it was unnecessary to add the extra expanded worlds tab in the Social menu and it should be reconsidered.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
